> drwxr-xr-x   2 root root    8.0K Mar 20  2003 TT_DB
> drwxr-xr-x  12 root root    8.0K Mar  3 13:11 people
> -rw-r-----   1 root dialout  16M Aug 12  2003 quota.group
> -rw-r-----   1 root dialout 256G Feb 24 15:04 quota.user
> 
> Has anyone heared of something like this yet?
> It might have happend after I ran a defragment on the driver but I'm not 
> sure about that...
> 
> Wimmy

quota.user is a sparse file.  You need to look at it with ls -s to 
see that actual storage allocated.  Or with the showfile command.

quota entries in the file are stored at the User ID number times 
the size of a quota structure.

It is my guess that a UID of somewhere in the neighborhood of 
0x80000000 more or less was used to create a file.  Maybe the 
nobody account often used by NFS for anonymous guest users has a 
0x80000000 or 0x7fffffff or 0x7ffffffe type value (or something in 
that neighborhood).

                                        Bob Harris


